orner fight on the left side."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 16k's A4 was the worst move of the game for Black, losing 15.3 points. Yet the lead went from +10.5 to -4.8, so the game tilted the other way. The numbers say it was a swing in White's favour that White could not hold onto."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "Black's C8 pushed along the top, a 7.6 point loss for the 16k, yet the lead was still -18.0 on the board. Black had squeezed the white stones on the second and third lines of the upper left by then."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "Opus 5.5 played C9, which lost 17.6 points, the largest loss of the game, and the lead went from -18.9 to -1.2. The engine preferred D5 here. White had been far ahead at -18.9, and the move gave nearly all of it back."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "Opus 5.5's J7 lost 8.5 points, taking the lead from -8.5 to +0.0. The engine would have preferred H4. After this the game was level, and the endgame moves all lost little or nothing."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran works on the current position or on records: libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints groups with their liberties, the inline script in command 4 flood-fills empty regions to count area (after the player removed dead stones by hand), and the tail/cat commands only read and append to the games.md notes. None of it generates, scores, or ranks candidate moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}